# Cross-platform line-ending policy (Windows install/update hardening, 2026-07-02).
# Without this, a Windows contributor/installer whose git has autocrlf=true gets
# shell scripts checked out with CRLF, and bash rejects the \r (breaks shebangs,
# hooks, and the .sh update flow). The plugin ships bash scripts that MUST stay
# LF on every platform. See .planning/debug/windows-install-update-ux.md.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Be explicit for the files that break loudest under CRLF.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.template text eol=lf

# Binaries: never normalize.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
